e se evalúa durante la evaluación de la deglución (VED) debido a su importancia en este proceso. Su función en la deglución puede verse afectada por diversas condiciones que pueden llevar a la disfagia, un trastorno que dificulta la capacidad de tragar.", "EPIGLOTIS:La epiglotis es una estructura que bloquea la laringe durante la deglución, asegurando que el bolo alimenticio se dirija al esófago.", "PALADAR:El paladar es la parte superior de la boca que ayuda a cerrar la cavidad nasal durante la deglución.", "NERVIOS CRANEALES:Los nervios craneales son un grupo de nervios que proporcionan la inervación necesaria para los músculos involucrados en la deglución.", "FARINGE:The entity \"FARINGE,\" also known as the pharynx, is a critical anatomical structure involved in the swallowing process. It is a muscular tube that connects the mouth and nasal passages to the esophagus, playing a vital role in the act of swallowing. The pharynx is assessed during procedures such as video fluoroscopy and VED (Videofluoroscopic Evaluation of Swallowing), highlighting its importance in evaluating swallowing function. Overall, the pharynx is an essential part of the throat that facilitates the transition of food and air, underscoring its significance in both respiratory and digestive systems.", "NÚCLEO DEL TRACTO SOLITARIO:El núcleo del tracto solitario es una estructura en el sistema nervioso central que juega un papel crucial en la deglución y la integración de información sensorial relacionada con este proceso.", "CEREBRO:CEREBRO refers to the brain, a central organ of the nervous system that plays a crucial role in regulating various functions, including swallowing and respiration. It is significantly impacted in patients with adrenoleukodystrophy due to inflammatory responses. Additionally, the brain is involved in various biochemical processes, including those related to copper metabolism. In the context of Wilson's disease, the brain is another critical organ affected, as copper accumulation can lead to neurological symptoms. Overall, CEREBRO encompasses the complex functions and vulnerabilities of the brain in relation to different medical conditions.", "ACCIDENTE CEREBROVASCULAR:A cerebrovascular accident (commonly known as a stroke) is a medical event that can significantly impact a person's ability to swallow, a condition known as dysphagia. This occurs due to damage to the brain areas responsible for swallowing, which is a direct result of interrupted blood flow to the brain. As a consequence of dysphagia, patients who have experienced a cerebrovascular accident are at an increased risk of developing aspiration pneumonia, a serious complication that arises when food or liquid enters the lungs.", "RESONANCIA MAGNÉTICA:Resonancia Magnética, or Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI), is a non-invasive diagnostic technique utilized for various medical purposes. It is primarily known for its application in studying brain activity and its relationship with functions such as swallowing and other neurological processes. Additionally, MRI serves as an important tool for quantifying liver iron concentration and assessing liver damage, particularly in patients suffering from hereditary hemochromatosis. This versatility highlights the significance of Resonancia Magnética in both neurological and hepatic evaluations.", "ESTIMULACIÓN MAGNÉTICA TRANSCRANEAL:La estimulación magnética transcraneal es una técnica que permite investigar la función cerebral y su implicación en procesos como la deglución.", "FORMACIÓN RETICULAR:La formación reticular es una estructura en el tronco del encéfalo que juega un papel importante en la regulación de la deglución y la respiración.", "GANGLIOS BASALES:Los ganglios basales son un grupo de núcleos en el cerebro que están implicados en el control motor y pueden influir en la deglución."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0,